---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Dashboard | API Error Response",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  The JSON body every API endpoint here answers an error with. The caller sets the real
  HTTP status with response_status first, and passes the same number as status_code.
  Called with:
    response_status 422
    render 'api/error_response', error_type: 'validation', errors: errors, status_code: 422
  errors: a hash of field name to a list of messages.
  The hash is printed as it is: on a JSON page the platform writes it out as JSON.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign response = {}
  assign response['success'] = false
  assign response['errors'] = errors | default: {}
  assign response['error_type'] = error_type | default: 'validation'
  assign response['status_code'] = status_code | default: 400
  assign response['valid'] = false
-%}
{{ response }}
